A||||3||My7Fieros||Door sags........||||1||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||06-17-2000||03:43 AM||||My drivers side door drops some when opening it..making closing it a little more effort. Also sometimes the weatherstripping gets pushed out by the window. Is there an "easy" way to fix this, or do I need to get a new lower hinge? Is that hard to replace? TIA, Brian||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||06-17-2000||07:30 AM||||Without being able to see it, this is just a guess.  With the door open, grab it from the back(where latch is)and see if you can move it up and down.  If you can feel "notchy" travel, chances are the pin bushings are wore out.<P>The uppers usually go first, but have seen the bottoms go too.<P>It generaly is the bushings and not the pins or hinges themselves.<P>Most parts houses carry the bushings; Pontiac sells them, and they aren't that hard to install.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Have a good one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-17-2000||09:18 AM||||It is possible that the hinges have either slipped slightly or weren't positioned correctly from the factory.  My door drops slightly when I open it but I can't move it at all (from the rear of the door).  I don't think there is much room for adjustment in the hinges, but there must be some play/slop.  Sometime (whenever I decide I really need to remove the trim again) I'll try to loosen the top hinge and pull the door up, then retighten the hinge.  Anyone know if there's a torque rating for the hinge bolts?||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||06-17-2000||02:38 PM||||I improved my sagging door by replacing the two upper bronze bushings($1.68)without removing the door,just supporting it while I removed(pounded out)the pins.<BR>I still need to take the front fender off and replace more parts to get it to stop rattling over bumps.||||reg||1
